From: CAT S22 build <builder@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:14:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActionBarOverlayLayout: keep content below a non-overlay
 action bar edge to edge

Since Android 15 windows are edge to edge. ActionBarOverlayLayout then only
reports the action bar height in the insets it dispatches and leaves the
content at the top of the window, so apps that never inset themselves for
the action bar (Emergency Info and other AOSP apps) show their first item
under the title. When the action bar is not in overlay mode, put the
content below it and remove that area from the dispatched insets, as for
windows that fit system windows. Windows that ask for a stable layout
(Settings) or hide the action bar keep the AOSP behaviour.

Change-Id: I1670951a6635674dd01bf5f9e63ea202ae73ae56

diff --git a/core/java/com/android/internal/widget/ActionBarOverlayLayout.java b/core/java/com/android/internal/widget/ActionBarOverlayLayout.java
index ff57fd4fe..2415f3a87 100644
--- a/core/java/com/android/internal/widget/ActionBarOverlayLayout.java
+++ b/core/java/com/android/internal/widget/ActionBarOverlayLayout.java
@@ -503,6 +503,18 @@ public class ActionBarOverlayLayout extends ViewGroup implements DecorContentPar
             }
             // Content view has been shrunk, shrink all insets to match.
             mInnerInsets = mInnerInsets.inset(0 /* left */, topInset, 0 /* right */, bottomInset);
+        } else if (!mOverlayMode && !stable && !mDecorFitsSystemWindows
+                && mActionBarTop.getVisibility() != GONE) {
+            // Edge-to-edge window (enforced from Android 15) that did not ask for an
+            // overlaid action bar: the action bar already covers the system bars, so keep
+            // the content below it instead of leaving the first item under the title, and
+            // tell the content that the area is taken. Older apps (Emergency Info and other
+            // AOSP apps on small screens) never inset themselves for the action bar.
+            // Windows with LAYOUT_STABLE (Settings) and hidden action bars keep the AOSP
+            // behaviour: there the reserved height does not mean a visible bar.
+            mContentInsets.top = Math.max(mContentInsets.top, topInset);
+            mContentInsets.bottom = Math.max(mContentInsets.bottom, bottomInset);
+            mInnerInsets = mInnerInsets.inset(0 /* left */, topInset, 0 /* right */, bottomInset);
         } else {
             // Add ActionBar to system window inset, but leave other insets untouched.
             if (mActionBarExtendsIntoSystemInsets) {
